# Lines `make qemu-test` must see on the serial console, in this order, as
# whole lines (NoWayOS's tools/qemu-test). The application starts, learns the
# screen and shows its first screen; then starter.qmp types a name and
# presses Continue, and Start again.
STARTER: ui: starting
STARTER: ui: the display is 1920x1080 at scale 2
STARTER: ui: showing welcome
STARTER: ui: pressed Continue
STARTER: ui: showing hello
STARTER: ui: pressed Start again
STARTER: ui: showing welcome

# Output that fails the test at once if it appears anywhere: a fault reported
# by the Microkit monitor, a kernel error, a panic, a PD giving up, a record
# refused or rejected, or input dropped anywhere - and the name the script
# types, which the log must never hold.
!MON|ERROR
!seL4(CPU
!panicked
!gave up
!refused
!rejected
!dropped so far
!over its rate
!the UI's ring is full
!zqvj
